The Python adaptation, converted R-fitted numerical assets, and parity fixtures
are distributed under `GPL-2.0-or-later`. The unchanged source archive is
retained under `vendor/` for provenance and live-reference installation.

The package is intentionally a separate optional distribution from the
Apache-2.0 `bijux-pollenomics` host project. Integrators must review the licence
consequences of distribution and deployment; the package metadata does not
assert that combining or redistributing the two projects creates no additional
obligations.

The stored LSM model assets originate from serialized models in the reference
archive. Native LOESS evaluation and refitting code was developed to reproduce
those numerical responses. The parity documentation states exactly what has and
has not been executed.
